CREATED:20261109T212507Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109T212507Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_317516751@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261128T073241Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T140000
SUMMARY:City Place and Toronto's Historic Rail Lands! (NEW FOR 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n**The Toronto History Walks Yearly Pass
  is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\, emai
 l**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for sign
 ing up!**\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount whe
 n booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following em
 ail at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nBefore the soaring condomi
 nium towers\, landscaped parks\, trendy cafés and bustling streets of Cit
 yPlace\, you would have found yourself standing in the middle of one of To
 ronto's busiest railway landscapes!\n\nFor generations\, this was a world 
 of locomotives\, freight trains\, railway workers\, industrial buildings a
 nd miles of track stretching across the waterfront. These were the Railway
  Lands.\n\nAn enormous piece of Toronto's industrial heartland that helped
  keep the city moving and connected to the rest of Canada. But as the rail
 ways changed and their operations disappeared\, an opportunity emerged: wh
 at would Toronto do with all this land?\n\nThe story of CityPlace is a sto
 ry about ambition\, controversy\, urban planning and the ever-changing fac
 e of Toronto. From the grand redevelopment visions of the 1960s\, the arri
 val of the CN Tower and SkyDome\, to the plans that transformed these form
 er railway yards into one of Canada's most recognizable residential commun
 ities\, CityPlace has quite a story to tell.\n\nWe'll explore how an indus
 trial wasteland became a forest of condominium towers\, and how Toronto re
 connected with its waterfront\, and how an entirely new neighbourhood was 
 created virtually from scratch.\n\nLet's discover CityPlace\, a new neighb
 ourhood that many Torontonians know today in passing. A fascinating histor
 y overlooked. We'll look beyond the glass towers and modern architecture t
 o uncover the railway history\, the ambitious plans\, the personalities an
 d the decisions that shaped this corner of the city.\n\nToronto is constan
 tly reinventing itself\, but sometimes you have to look beneath the street
 s\, and even beneath the buildings\, to understand how it happened. Come a
 nd discover the remarkable transformation!\n\nThis walking tour begins at 
 Toronto Public Library - Fort York Branch\, at the corner of Bathurst Stre
 et and Fort York Blvd. The Bathurst Streetcar stops at the corner. We end 
 at The Well at the corner of Spadina and Front.\n\nThis walking tour is fo
 r all walking levels. Please dress for the season\, and hope to see you th
 ere.\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 per person.\n\n\\*\\* **Ple
 ase note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for 
 this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohisto
 rywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/317516
 751/
